In a series of prompts, James requested technical summaries for various sections of a report, including agriculture, coastal impacts, and flooding. The goal was to create concise summaries focusing on methodologies while avoiding references to figures, tables, or results from the original paper. The summaries outlined the modeling approaches used for assessing impacts on agriculture from climate change, combining multiple models into a single estimate, and for coastal impacts and flooding, detailing the use of specific models (CIAM, DIVA, LISFLOOD) and methods of uncertainty calibration. In each case, the summaries emphasized Bayesian meta-analysis and the treatment of adaptation uncertainty, with references to the original work (cited as rising2026comprehensive) for additional details.
